573 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 232 0 R /Rect [ 56.723999 445.643954 283.523987 745.883944 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure3) /TU (Flowchart illustrating a neural network architecture. The input token \\\(E_{token}\\\) with dimensions \\\([B, N, D]\\\) splits into three branches through Linear layers labeled Q, K, and V, each with dimensions \\\([B, N, H, d]\\\). Matrices K and Q interact to form S \\\([B, H, N, N]\\\), which undergoes a Softmax transformation. The resulting matrix multiplies with V, yielding \\\(V_{attn}\\\) \\\([B, N, D]\\\). This output feeds into the "KAN layer.") /Type /Annot >>
endobj
574 0 obj
<< /BS << /W 0 >> /F 4 /FT /Btn /Ff 65536 /MK << /BC [ 0 0 0 0 ] >> /P 232 0 R /Rect [ 311.666992 456.64197 538.453003 745.727969 ] /Subtype /Widget /T (Figure4) /TU (Flowchart of a neural network architecture with labeled components and paths. It includes inputs like \\\( V_{\\text{attn}} \\\) and \\\( G \\\), processing through SiLU, B-spline basis functions, and operations generating outputs \\\( Y_{\\text{fused}} \\\) and \\\( Y \\\). Various layers and matrix shapes are indicated at each step.) /Type /Annot >>
endobj
